### Q79. Measurement Error

**Question:** A measuring instrument has accuracy specification ±(0.5% of reading + 2 digits). If it displays 2.000 V (3 decimal digits), the maximum absolute error is approximately:

(a) ±0.002 V  
(b) ±0.010 V  
(c) ±0.012 V  
(d) ±0.020 V

**Answer: (c) ±0.012 V**

**Solution:**

\[
\text{Error} = 0.5\% \text{ of } 2.000 + 2 \text{ digits}
\]
\[
= 0.005 \times 2.000 + 0.002 = 0.010 + 0.002 = 0.012V
\]

**Alternative Questions:**
1. What is the percentage error? **(0.6%)**
2. What is the resolution? **(0.001 V)**

