### Q49. Power Factor Correction

**Question:** A distribution feeder has power factor 0.7 lagging. To improve to 0.95 lagging by shunt capacitor bank at the load consuming S = 100kVA, what kvar of capacitor is needed approximately? (approximate using \( Q_{new} = P(\tan\phi_1 - \tan\phi_2) \))

(a) \( Q_c ≈ P(\tan\cos^{-1}0.7 - \tan\cos^{-1}0.95) \) - numeric approx 60 kvar  
(b) \( Q_c ≈ 100(\tan\cos^{-1}0.7 - \tan\cos^{-1}0.95) = 40 kvar \)  
(c) \( Q_c ≈ 100 \times 0.5 = 50 kvar \)  
(d) \( Q_c ≈ 10 kvar \)

**Answer: (c) \( Q_c \approx 50\ kvar \)**

**Solution:**

\[
P = S \cos\phi_1 = 100 \times 0.7 = 70kW
\]
\[
\phi_1 = \cos^{-1}(0.7) = 45.57°, \tan\phi_1 = 1.02
\]
\[
\phi_2 = \cos^{-1}(0.95) = 18.19°, \tan\phi_2 = 0.329
\]
\[
Q_c = P(\tan\phi_1 - \tan\phi_2) = 70(1.02 - 0.329) = 70 \times 0.691 = 48.4 kvar
\]

Closest option is (b) 40 kvar or (c) 50 kvar. The closest is (c) 50 kvar.

**Alternative Questions:**
1. What is the new apparent power? **(\( S = P/\cos\phi_2 = 70/0.95 = 73.7 kVA \))**
2. What is the reduction in line current? **(\( \Delta I = (S_1 - S_2)/V \))**

