### Q64. Oscilloscope RMS Value

**Question:** An oscilloscope with vertical sensitivity 10mV/div displays a sine wave spanning 4 divisions peak-to-peak. The RMS value of the sine wave is:

(a) \( 10mV/div \times 4/2 \times 1/\sqrt{2} = 14.14mV \)  
(b) 20 mV  
(c) 28.3 mV  
(d) 10 mV

**Answer: (a) \( 14.14mV \)**

**Solution:**

Peak-to-peak = 4 divisions × 10 mV/div = 40 mV  
Peak = 40/2 = 20 mV  
RMS = \( 20/\sqrt{2} = 14.14 mV \)

**Alternative Questions:**
1. What is the peak value? **(20 mV)**
2. What is the average value? **(0, for sine wave)**

