### Q66. Phase Measurement on Oscilloscope

**Question:** Phase measurement: Two sinusoidal voltages of same frequency have phase difference of 30°. On dual-trace oscilloscope with timebase such that period is 10 divisions, the time shift between traces will be:

(a) \( 30°/360° \times 10 = 0.833 \) divisions  
(b) \( 30/360 \times 10 = 0.833 \) divisions  
(c) 1 division  
(d) 0.5 division

**Answer: (a) and (b) are the same: 0.833 divisions**

**Solution:**

\[
\text{Time shift} = \frac{\phi}{360°} \times T = \frac{30°}{360°} \times 10 = 0.833 \text{ divisions}
\]

**Alternative Questions:**
1. What is the time shift if phase is 90°? **(2.5 divisions)**
2. What is the phase if time shift is 1 division? **(36°)**

