### Q67. Power Measurement

**Question:** A power meter measures active power P and reactive power Q. For a single-phase load with \( V_{rms} = 230V, I_{rms} = 10A \) and power factor 0.6 lagging, compute P and Q.

(a) P = 1380W, Q = 1840 var  
(b) P = 2300W, Q = 2300 var  
(c) P = 1380W, Q = 1840 var (same as a)  
(d) P = 2300W, Q = 1380 var

**Answer: (a) P = 1380W, Q = 1840 var**

**Solution:**

\[
P = VI\cos\phi = 230 \times 10 \times 0.6 = 1380W
\]
\[
Q = VI\sin\phi = 230 \times 10 \times 0.8 = 1840 VAR
\]

**Alternative Questions:**
1. What is the apparent power? **(2300 VA)**
2. What is the power factor angle? **(53.13°)**

