### Q70. Transistor Amplifier Q-Point

**Question:** A transistor amplifier has \( R_C = 2kΩ, V_{CC} = 12V \). If collector current \( I_C = 2mA \) at Q-point, what is collector-emitter voltage \( V_{CE} \) (neglect saturation)?

(a) \( V_{CE} = 12 - I_C R_C = 12 - 4 = 8V \)  
(b) \( V_{CE} = 4V \)  
(c) \( V_{CE} = 12V \)  
(d) \( V_{CE} = 8.5V \)

**Answer: (a) \( V_{CE} = 8V \)**

**Solution:**

\[
V_{CE} = V_{CC} - I_C R_C = 12 - 2 \times 10^{-3} \times 2 \times 10^3 = 12 - 4 = 8V
\]

**Alternative Questions:**
1. What is the power dissipated? **(\( P = V_{CE} I_C = 16 mW \))**
2. What is the maximum swing? **(8 V peak-to-peak)**

