### Q42. DC Shunt Motor Back EMF

**Question:** A DC shunt motor has armature resistance \( R_a = 0.05Ω \) and field flux constant. At no-load speed 1500rpm armature current is negligible. When loaded at 1000rpm, armature current measured 80A with terminal voltage 220V. Back EMF \( E_b \) approximate is:

(a) \( 220 - 80 \times 0.05 = 216V \)  
(b) \( 220 - 4 = 216V \)  
(c) \( 220 - 80 = 140V \)  
(d) \( 220V \)

**Answer: (a) and (b) are the same: \( E_b = 216V \)**

**Solution:**

\[
E_b = V - I_a R_a = 220 - 80 \times 0.05 = 220 - 4 = 216V
\]

